raordinary cast uh they've  all done very well  uh is there anyone who has surprised me  though  um i don't know i  in a sense i suppose all all three of  the principal children were surprises  they were the hardest roles to cast  it's really hard to find good kid actors  there are a lot of kid actors in the  world and  including in london and ireland where we  principally conducted our search for our  arya our sansa and our brand  um but most kids you know it's a great  it's hard for a kid to memorize all  these long speeches you know and  and uh you so you you get kids in and  they've memorized the lines  but that's all they've done you know  there's nothing they're not acting  they're just reciting lines that they've  memorized and i don't  i'm not trying to criticize for that  it's it's a great achievement for a  nine-year-old kid to to do something  like that but uh  that doesn't mean they can carry off the  role and then on the other hand you get  the other extreme you get sort of the  uh the the kid actor who has been taught  maybe he has taken a few  drama classes in school and he's been  taught that acting is all about emoting  so they emote all over the place they're  grimacing and  grinning and making faces and it's you  know you just want to tell them to stop  it you know  stop mugging for the camera it's way way  too much  and you know you look at hundreds of  these auditions and you begin to despair  of ever finding it  and then we find someone like maisie  with the minute i saw maisie williams  edition i knew she was arya  and uh david and dan all agreed i mean  she was she was just perfect  and sophie turner isaac hempstead right  there they're  doing amazing too and you know most kid  actors in hollywood there's a lot of  them on sitcoms that come out of  los angeles but all they have to really  do is be cute  and kind of get off a snappy one-liner  occasionally that  puts down the adults um that's the usual  sitcom formula  um our kids have to do a